    "sourceCommit": "971deb085f25f8f8b4ed34e0097e1c62e59a83f0",
    "text": "Build 39 \u2014 photographer / videographer client listings.\n\nIn real estate onboarding choose Agent or Photographer / videographer. Existing accounts can change this in Settings \u2192 Real estate workflow.\n\nCreate a listing, then open Listing contact. Choose My client and enter the realtor/business name, brokerage, phone, public email and client photo. A separate private email can receive inquiries. Save before publishing. My account explicitly uses your own card instead.\n\nPublish two of your own test listings with different contacts. Verify each marketing page shows only its intended client. Hide Rendprop logos and app promotions if desired; the service domain/privacy disclosure remain. The MLS link omits contacts and inquiry forms.\n\nOpen the same listing in Studio \u2192 Create & publish \u2192 Details. Check the saved card, edit it, then reopen on the phone. Conflicting or unsaved changes must be resolved before publishing; interrupted saves must retain the draft and reuse a successful photo upload.\n\nSubmit an inquiry on your own test listing using an email you control. Check Leads and the intended inbox. The inquiry stays in the photographer account; Email sent means provider acceptance, not guaranteed inbox placement. Review the current recipient and explicitly resend once. Older inquiries use Send to client. Pending sends cancel when contact routing is disabled or changed; an already dispatched email cannot be recalled.\n\nCamera and actual cross-device/inbox behavior require your phone and controlled test accounts. Existing guided-room capture improvements remain included; room tours are still local exports and 3D reconstruction remains disabled.\n"
  },
